  "assumptions": [
    "Synthetic magnetic flux-density response only; not an observation correction or unique geological interpretation.",
    "Every point/source/moment/background shares one explicit local Cartesian metre frame, x/y/up axes and height datum; caller performs upstream coordinate/north/datum conversion.",
    "Moments in A*m^2 are independent signed vector components. No induced-only direction, susceptibility, volume, IGRF, demagnetisation or finite-body interior is inferred.",
    "A caller-selected positive exclusion distance applies to every dipole, including zero moments; no softening or clipping.",
    "With explicit nonzero background, linear TMI projects the SUMMED vector on its direction; exact TMI is the magnitude difference after superposition and is not additive. Without background, TMI outputs are null.",
    "Sensitivities are fixed-position/background moment-component derivatives of vectors and LINEAR TMI only; no exact-TMI or geometry derivatives, inversion or uncertainty propagation.",
    "The linearization difference and response/background ratio diagnose approximation behaviour, not calibrated uncertainty. Pinned CODATA2022 permeability measurement uncertainty is not propagated."
  ],
